{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And may he rule</b> — if concerning Solomon, [from] the Sea — [to] its end." "<b>to the Sea</b> — Philistines." "<b>and from the River</b> — this is the Euphrates." "<b>and to the ends of the earth</b> — this is the desert. And so he mentioned the length of the land of Israel and its breadth." "And if concerning the Messiah: [from] the Sea — the southern [sea], called the Red Sea, to the northern sea, which is the Ocean Sea." "<b>and from the River</b> — the river that goes out from Eden, which is at the beginning of the east, <b>and to the ends of the earth</b>, which is at the end of the west."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 72, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:00.511678761Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}